# Machine-readable citation file for the VERIFY Framework.
# Format: Citation File Format 1.2.0 — https://citation-file-format.github.io
# Validated against the CFF schema before each release.

cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Teaching AI to Ask: The VERIFY Framework"
message: "If you use VERIFY in research, curriculum, or another publication, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Robinson
    given-names: Sandra
    affiliation: "Big Wella"
    website: "https://bigwella.com"
abstract: >-
  VERIFY is an AI literacy framework for secondary and adult learners and the people who teach them.
  It names six steps — Validate, Examine, Reflect, Investigate, Filter, Your judgement —
  and gives teachers the practitioner moves to make each step happen in their classroom.
  The framework is grounded in cognitive science (cognitive offloading, productive struggle,
  metacognitive laziness, Meta-Task Awareness, the illusion of mastery) and in Australian
  classroom equity research. The repository contains the full Teacher Guide, two assessment
  rubrics (A–E and four-level), an interactive walk-through tool for use alongside a teacher,
  and a Claude skill file.
keywords:
  - AI literacy
  - generative AI in education
  - secondary education
  - adult education
  - lifelong learning
  - Australian education
  - metacognition
  - productive struggle
  - cognitive offloading
  - critical thinking
  - assessment
  - teacher professional learning
